"Andrew bakes 200 mini cinnamon rolls and does not bake 300 mini blueberry muffins. A normal cinnamon roll has 600 calories and a normal blueberry muffin has 450 calories. If a mini pastry has 1/3rd of the calories of a normal version, how many calories do the pastries he baked have?","Andrew bakes 200 mini cinnamon rolls and 300 mini blueberry muffins. A normal cinnamon roll has 600 calories and a normal blueberry muffin has 450 calories. If a mini pastry has 1/3rd of the calories of a normal version, how many calories do the pastries he baked have?",85000,85000,400,850,"To solve the problem step by step:

1. **Understand the problem**: Andrew bakes 200 mini cinnamon rolls and does not bake 300 mini blueberry muffins. We need to calculate the total calories of the pastries he baked.

